1. Understand the Target Types
PyRIT distinguishes between:

PromptTarget: A general endpoint for sending prompts.

PromptChatTarget: A subclass that supports conversation history, system messages, etc.
azure.github.io

Depending on whether your target is conversational (like a chat API) or one-off (like a simple HTTP endpoint), you’ll choose the appropriate base.

2. Review the Official Documentation
In the “Creating Custom Targets” section of PyRIT’s docs, there’s a tutorial demonstrating how to connect to "Gandalf" and "Crucible" targets. These examples show how to write your own target that plugs into PyRIT's orchestrators and scorers—definitely worth checking out!
